<DESC><![CDATA[The Security Council,

Chronicling the story of [nation]Gagium[/nation], a complicated nation that sprang into existence in 2017. They first entered [region]The League[/region] &amp; [region]Concord[/region] in 2020 and later triumphantly returned in 2023 when they helped The League silence a former rival, the Federation of Conservative Nations,

Initially hopeful for this nation&#146;s future as they began their modern career in 2022 by participating in the anti-fascist invasion of Confederacy of Layem as a precursor event to their journey back to The League &amp; Concord, aiding in destroying the Republic&#146;s longtime enemy,

Concerned that upon reentry to The League, Gagium was swiftly elevated to Director of Culture. It was from there they orchestrated the spread of neo-moralist thought to the populace of The League &amp; Concord through several wicked carnivals both during and following their tenure as Director, including:

[list][*]Overseeing festivals for the eighth, ninth, and tenth anniversary of The League &amp; Concord&#146;s founding, celebrating the draconian regime and eventual rule through various contests, events, and displays honoring their own cult of personality,
[*]Subjecting various citizens of nations in The League &amp; Concord to gruesome &#147;hunger games&#148; events with intricate maps and treasures throughout the arena, pitting comrades against one another to fight for Gagium&#146;s amusement,
[*]Overhauling the regions&#146; dispatches and guides, ensuring their cult of personality maintained a monopoly of information throughout the Republic, and indoctrinating countless nations to their causes,[/list]

Nauseated by Gagium&#146;s later ascension as Consul of the Republic in January 2025 (and Chief Consul in November 2025), making them one of the regions&#146; heads of state and furthering their influence over the Republic to near-measurable extents,

Recoiling at the diplomatic trickery accomplished by Gagium on the Consulate, where they successfully deceived several regions into entering formal treaties and memoranda with their government, notably:

[list][*]The Treaty of Delvin-Paluri with Talonia, acquired through backdoor negotiations between Gagium and Moukden and Kirin enabled by their unique relationship, leading the regions to enter a formal alliance which would see two autocracies collaborate on draconian governance and anti-Sinkerite discrimination, 
[*]Twice as Bright with The West Pacific, a region which itself includes many condemned nations, this alliance allowing both regions to continue to zealously advance the dismantling of the General Assembly, 
[*]Their key role in the diplomatic conversion of (and eventual alliance with) Starlight &amp; Horizon, emboldening the neo-moralist and national sovereigntist movements by strategizing with allies on how to bring the regime into the fold of the new world order,[/list]

Dismayed by Gagium&#146;s military exploits, subverting a Defender region into a brutal and efficient war machine. Gagium swept over numerous regions, earning themselves the censure of being named &#147;Raider of the Year&#148; by the international community as a result of their most high-profile crimes,

[list][*]Their infamy as &#147;the Butcher of Frutiger,&#148; planning, supervising, and executing The League&#146;s Defense Forces&#146; occupation of the small Frontier, leading to it becoming a trophy possession of their Consulate,
[*]Decimation of New Welgard, which was used to train officers under Gagium&#146;s tutelage in the practices of military cruelty,[/list]

Loathing Gagium&#146;s despotic [i]magnum opus[/i] in New United Kingdom, where they oversaw the largest Frontier annexation to-date. Shortly after retiring as WA Delegate of The League under the pretext of enlisting to defend innocent nations, they entered New United Kingdom as [nation]Adieux[/nation] and were installed by the outgoing leadership as &#147;Vice Delegate&#148; to enforce the region&#146;s annexation into Concord. There, they silenced opposition and ensured the conquest was completed, never facing trial for their crimes,

Horrified by Gagium&#39;s pivotal role in a constitutional crisis in The League &amp; Concord in June of 2026 which threatened to tear the Republic asunder. When Gagium and their co-conspirators in the rogue Consulate were deposed by the Committee to Preserve the Republic, it was thought that the world would be safe from Gagium&#39;s machinations,

Shocked that Gagium would once again trade allegiances, aiding the new government of The League &amp; Concord in various intelligence pursuits. Their work aided the Consulate in zealously identifying information leaks, pursuing subversives abroad, and ultimately bringing a close to the June constitutional crisis via reunification with Eladria under a common Republic,

Surmising that this nation&#146;s path tells a fascinating story worthy of recognition, and that a condemnation is the most fitting form to define their memory,

Hereby condemns [nation=long]Gagium[/nation].]]></DESC>
